From eb8fb65bf29cae69f62a4e81142065a375ab4ba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:05:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): opt-in hover raises via [input.focus]
 hover_raises

follows_mouse hovering raises the entered window as it focuses, so sweeping
the cursor across a larger window underneath buries the window above it.
hover_raises = false narrows a hover to focus alone: clicks, keybinds, and
activation keep raising. The default stays true, and the key is inert without
follows_mouse.

Raise is decided once in FocusManager::focusView and threaded through
View::applySeatFocus and Workspace::setFocusedView, so the scene order and
the floating stack move together and a later restack cannot replay a stale
order. Only FocusReason::PointerHover is special; every other focus reason
raises exactly as before. retainCurrentKeyboardFocus replays the last raise
decision instead of guessing, so a focus kept through a popup grab restacks
the way the transition that selected it did.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
